{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqr2jk9hawd","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"code graph llm retrieval feature shipped to main fixes the agentic code retrieval hole","summary":"The production hole (agentic search abstains on code because the relevance decision is a heuristic threshold with no code-tier calibration, and code_nodes were RAG-only / never judged) is now addressed on main (merge commit 8ea3d203). The code-graph-llm-retrieval feature shipped 5 pieces: (1) AST call/import edges persisted as a deterministic code_edges overlay layer, separate from the task DAG (no judge — code edges are ground truth); (2) retrieval surfaces structural neighbors (callers/callees/imports) ADDITIVELY with bounded fan-out; (3) a standalone LLM grader module (intent-aware continue/reformulate/keep/abstain/aggregate, in-process backend); (4) the grader wired into runAgenticContextSearches as an ADDITIVE, floor-preserving controller — judge #9 formally traced that the output is provably superset-or-equal to the single-shot+structural floor (added candidates drawn only from the rejected set; union never drops a floor member; abstain gate bypassed on the grader path), so the 0.346 abstention regression is structurally impossible; (5) fixed the search-context daemon wedge (a rerank-sidecar cold-start spawn storm — cooldown latch + EADDRINUSE guard). The grader path is feature-flagged OFF by default (ORCH_SEARCH_GRADER / use_grader, round cap default 4 ceiling 6); the wedge fix + code_edges layer are active. ACTIVATION on the live :8787 daemon needs a user-gated restart to load the new code. Built via the orchestrator (feature branch, 5 impl tasks + paired judges, attempt→feature→main); automode auto-merge was OFF so the dispatcher executed the tier-1 and tier-2 merges manually, and recovered one worker (#2) that stalled on a background test-suite wait by verifying its 26 tests + committing. The separate embed-enrich 0.705 embed fix remains pending its own gated main merge.","categor